  {
   "id": "lg_read",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1968,
   "width": 993.24,
   "height": 180.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2253,
   "version": 2,
   "versionNonce": 9253,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Each line starts on the FK column (yellow row) of the child table and ends on the key it\nreferences. Composite FKs (workspace_id, x_id) are drawn once, at the x_id column.\nGrey row = primary key. Blue row = logical reference without an FK constraint.\nLine colour = parent table: orange users, blue workspaces, green departments / chunks,\npurple documents, cyan categories, pink messages, indigo conversations, lime memberships.\nGrey dashed = logical link (no FK).  Amber dashed = across schemas / HTTP.\nOrange header = global table, no RLS.  Other headers: FORCE RLS on workspace_id.\nDashed table outline = approved in ADR-009, not in the migrations yet (V2-36).",
   "originalText": "Each line starts on the FK column (yellow row) of the child table and ends on the key it\nreferences. Composite FKs (workspace_id, x_id) are drawn once, at the x_id column.\nGrey row = primary key. Blue row = logical reference without an FK constraint.\nLine colour = parent table: orange users, blue workspaces, green departments / chunks,\npurple documents, cyan categories, pink messages, indigo conversations, lime memberships.\nGrey dashed = logical link (no FK).  Amber dashed = across schemas / HTTP.\nOrange header = global table, no RLS.  Other headers: FORCE RLS on workspace_id.\nDashed table outline = approved in ADR-009, not in the migrations yet (V2-36).",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
